okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Manage the rotating Codex/Claude OAuth tokens from the prelaunch menu UI instead of only `ciel-runtime tokens`."
reported: "User, 2026-09-30, after being told to use `ciel-runtime tokens login|import`: '무슨소리야.. ui로 생성하라고한게 언젠데'."
confirmed_before_change:
  existing: "f91af10 (2026-09-27) shipped the token store, rotation pool and the `ciel-runtime tokens` CLI only; no menu entry existed (MAIN_MENU_ACTIONS ended at web-backend)."
  request_record: "The UI request is not in docs/journal/2026/09/27/features/oauth-tokens/workspace-token-rotation.okf nor in the Claude/Codex transcripts searched; it was treated as the user states."
change:
  panel_module: "ciel_runtime_support/oauth_token_menu.py: panel_rows(workspace_state_dir) lists every stored token (provider, label, state active/draining/limited/disabled, usage windows, id; never the secret) plus '+ Sign in Codex/Claude (browser)', '+ Import Codex/Claude (<default credentials path>)', 'Back'. apply() drives the same run_tokens_command as the CLI: login (asks a label; browser progress printed to the terminal), import (asks path with the CLI's default, then label), token row (asks disable / enable / refresh / remove). CLI SystemExit and exceptions become panel messages; multi-line notes are split one per row."
  menu: "prelaunch.MAIN_MENU_ACTIONS gains 'oauth-tokens' before quit; open_panel/handler branches in prelaunch.py (line mode restored around prompts and the browser sign-in); main row '15. OAuth tokens  [N stored · Codex/Claude rotation]' (prelaunch_panel_projection.oauth_tokens_summary); panel title 'OAuth tokens'."
verification:
  real_menu: "WSL tmux, `ciel_runtime.py cli` from the working tree with an isolated config: main menu shows '15. OAuth tokens  [none · Codex/Claude rotation]'; Enter opens 'OAuth tokens options' with the sign-in/import rows; '+ Import Claude' -> path prompt -> label 'team-main' -> row 'Claude  team-main  [active · no usage yet]  claude-…' and the import note on separate lines; token row -> 'disable' -> '[disabled · …]' and 'claude-… disabled.'; Left back to the main menu shows '15. OAuth tokens  [1 stored · Codex/Claude rotation]'. The access token string does not appear in plain text under the config dir."
  tests: "tests/test_oauth_token_menu.py (6): menu order, empty panel, two imports -> two rotating tokens without secrets in rows, disable/enable/remove, errors as messages, sign-in label and terminal progress. Updated pins: test_request_limits_config (-4/-3/-2), test_prelaunch_panel_projection (row 15). WSL groups: unit 1672 OK, router 1158 OK, channel 438 OK, runtime 327 OK; ruff clean."
  not_run: "Browser sign-in against the real OpenAI/Anthropic endpoints (needs a person to complete the login); the login path is covered with an injected runner."
